## Skin care

- use emollients every day, especially after washing
- have lukewarm baths and showers, and pat skin dry
- try not to scratch or pick at scales

## Triggers

Keep a diary of flare-ups to spot triggers, such as stress, illness or skin injury.

## Sunlight

Some people find sunlight helps, but avoid sunburn, which can trigger psoriasis.

## Healthy living

- **stop smoking**, which can make psoriasis worse
- keep **alcohol** low
- look after your **heart**: stay active and have your blood pressure and cholesterol checked

## Your mental health

Skin conditions can affect confidence, relationships and mood. Anxiety and depression are more common in people with long-term skin conditions. Talk to your GP if you are struggling. You can refer yourself to **NHS Talking Therapies** in England. **Changing Faces** supports people with a visible difference.

## Support

The **Psoriasis Association** has information and an online community.
